WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:07.529
Speaker 1: We now have heard from former national
security adviser John Bolton and former attorney

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:11.500
to Donald Trump and friend of the show, Michael
Cohen.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.760
Both believe that Donald Trump probably has
won more documents at some of his other houses.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.670
And number two, even copies of the documents
that were seized by the FBI.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:29.160
And it really wouldn't be surprising that
both are true.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.720
Let's first listen to Trump's former national
security adviser, John Bolton.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.539
Not a guy that I like politically.

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:39.249
I think he is a depraved warmongering individual.

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:44.829
But I've not known him to be overtly dishonest
in interviews that he does when it comes to

00:00:44.829 --> 00:00:46.409
just basic factual matters.

00:00:46.409 --> 00:00:49.059
Sure, he'll distort about the case for war.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:50.850
He's done that before.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.909
But he has appeared to be completely straightforward,
at least on factual matters of this sort.

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:58.530
Take a listen to what he had to say when he
was interviewed.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.539
Speaker 2: Well, given that it's Donald Trump
we're talking about, I'm not surprised in

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:03.539
the slightest.

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:08.660
And I wouldn't be surprised if there were
more highly classified documents at Bedminster

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.780
or some some other residents of his.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.760
I just think it's important that everybody,
whether they're pro-Trump or anti-Trump or

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.730
whatever their position is, to try and take
a deep breath here and let this process play

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:20.730
out.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:26.030
You know, the filing that was done last night
in the United States, that included that picture

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:32.660
that you've shown there and a lot of information
about the documents and about Trump's obstruction

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:33.930
is the word they used.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:39.950
The refusal to turn them over to the National
Archives is revealing bit by bit the seriousness

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.600
of the case, and we don't know all the details
yet.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.550
It could be very, very serious.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:50.260
But my strong urging to everybody is stay
calm.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:51.260
Let's let it play out.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.780
We've got due process in the United States.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.310
The facts will come out here.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:59.750
But let's not jump to conclusions that the
Justice Department is an arm of the Democratic

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.450
Party on the one hand or the Trump to go to
jail tomorrow on the other.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.450
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:10.660
And of course, there's no evidence that this
Justice Department investigation is operating

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.730
at the direction of Joe Biden or any such
thing.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.240
Now, we heard something similar from Michael
Cohen.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.810
Michael Cohen tweeted, quote, I have been
saying since the FBI, I have been saying this

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.390
since the FBI raid.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:29.800
I believe Trump has copies, potentially other
documents as well at other locations, including

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.569
his children's homes.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:33.880
Weisselberg's Florida Home.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:41.410
Allen Weisselberg is the CFO now indicted
of Trump's business Bedminster, New Jersey

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.510
golf course, Fifth Avenue apartment, etc..

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:53.560
Now, if this is true and it's completely plausibly
true, there are probably foreign spies already

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.670
trying to infiltrate those locations with
how easy it has been for foreign agents to

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.900
get into Mar a Lago over the last few years.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.260
It would not be shocking at all that some
of our adversaries are already looking at

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.770
whether Donald Trump has other documents or
copies of documents that some of his other

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:16.230
homes and, you know, we talked earlier about
is the DOJ being political?

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:22.430
If they are deliberately waiting until after
the midterms to indict Trump, the more I learn,

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.960
the more it sounds like they're nowhere near
ready to charge because they may need to have

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.130
more search warrants.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:32.690
They may need to try to find documents at
other of Trump's homes.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.720
The way things are looking and at this point,
from a national security standpoint, it has

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.459
to be assumed that everything is compromised.

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:45.050
All of the at any of these documents that
Trump took, it has to be assumed that our

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.880
adversaries may have gotten their hands on
them.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:53.250
It has to be assumed that there are copies
because it's Trump, after all.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.780
And the person who is now trying to clean
up this mess but only making things worse,

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.000
is Donald Trump's spokeswoman, Liz Harrington.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:00.269
Let's talk about her next.

